# Standing demand: push the Standing Echo persistence frontier.
#
# The registry's best Standing Echo holds persistence 0.8679 (measured
# 2026-08-07, 1153 rows). This program demands one at >= 0.87 — a floor
# no existing primitive meets, sitting just past the all-time best, so
# it stays unresolved until evolutionary search genuinely advances the
# frontier. This is the KCB-1 research direction (close the delayed-
# identity gap = longer-lived structure) expressed as scheduler demand.
# Noise-tolerance floors are deliberately absent: the registry already
# saturates noise_tolerance at 1.0, so only persistence is a frontier.

cell FrontierEcho() {
    when always => base crystal.primitive "Standing Echo" min_persistence 0.87
}

grow FrontierEcho()
